notes = "Unofficial core: not affiliated with or endorsed by Microsoft. 64-BIT FRONTENDS ONLY: cartridge images are PXT64-only (the official pxt compiler has no 32-bit output and the runtime's PXT32 image patching is an unimplemented upstream TODO), so 32-bit builds can load but cannot run anything. Plays ONLY .pxt64 bytecode images - the file browser lists .pxt64 files only. MakeCode Arcade .png cartridges contain source code only, NOT a playable game: get a .pxt64 first - export it from the official IDE's experimental VM target, or batch-convert with cartconv (both documented at github.com/whmzsu/makecode-arcade-cartconv). Buttons are remappable under Quick Menu > Controls (Start = in-game menu, Select = reset); the core exposes no options."
